{"availability":"available","full":"DerekPaulHoffman/TeeTimeAI","name":"TeeTimeAI","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2025-05-06T13:54:49Z","updated":"2026-10-08T23:43:16Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://teetimeai.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://teetimeai.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:53.251Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:53.251Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:53.251Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:53.251Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Tee Time Spot is an alert-only availability assistant for public outdoor golf and verified public simulator rentals. The golfer books direct.","The product helps a golfer answer one practical question: \"Where can I play, at the courses I actually like, in the window I am free?\" A user enters a location and search distance (15 miles by default), picks nearby public courses, ranks 1 to 5 favorites, chooses a future date, time window, player count, and alert recipients, then receives an email when a matching tee time appears. The first check inspects each official course surface before classifying monitoring coverage. For dates beyond a course's booking window, Tee Time Spot records provider-confirmed release rules when available, tells…","Search windows are interpreted in each selected course's IANA timezone. The browser timezone is stored with the search for recipient-facing timestamps; instant alerts show the course-local time as the booking source of truth and also show the golfer's local time when it differs."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/DerekPaulHoffman/TeeTimeAI/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"32b63ec690212139d717c973d80059612f0e7518c7d40fd2fe30f63a518c1ae5","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:53.377Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:53.377Z","projectInsights":{"version"